course: dictionary
lesson: 4821
title: Hunter: more than one meaning
level: primary-4
stars: 0
explain: One word can have more than one meaning. The word hunter can mean a person who chases wild animals, an animal that catches other animals, or someone who searches hard for something. Context tells you which meaning is right, so look at the words around it.
explain: «Eagles are big birds of prey: hunters with hooked beaks, huge feet and amazing eyes.» Here a hunter is an animal, because the sentence talks about beaks and feet and birds of prey. The clue is the word birds. A hunter in this sentence is a predator, an animal that catches other animals.
explain: «Programmers are pattern hunters» does not mean people with guns. Ask yourself: what is being hunted? Here it is patterns, so a pattern hunter is someone who searches hard for patterns. When you know what is being searched for, you know the meaning.
fact: A hunter is a person or an animal that hunts, which means chases or searches to catch or find something.
fact: «Hunter» can mean a person who hunts wild animals for food or sport, as in «a skilled hunter».
fact: «Hunter» can mean an animal that catches other animals, like «Eagles are big birds of prey» or «Leopard seals are big hunters».
fact: «Hunter» can also mean someone who searches hard for something, as in «treasure hunter» or «bargain hunter».
fact: «Hunter-gatherer» describes early people who got food by hunting animals and gathering plants.
exercise: «Cats are hunters by instinct.» What does hunters mean in this sentence? | * An animal that catches other animals | A person who hunts wild animals for sport | Someone who searches for bargains | A team that plays football
exercise: A treasure hunter is someone who | Hunts wild animals for food | Sells jewellery in a shop | * Searches hard for gold or hidden things | Looks after a museum
exercise: «Camouflage means looking like your surroundings so that hunters, or the animals you hunt, do not notice you.» What does hunters mean here? | People or animals that chase and catch others | * People or animals that search or chase, which here means those who could catch you | Children playing a game of tag | Gardeners who cut hedges
test: «Leopard seals are big hunters with powerful jaws and long teeth that catch penguins.» What does hunters mean here? | Teachers who mark tests | * Animals that catch other animals, like predators | Shops that sell penguins | Animals that catch other animals
test: Ella says a hunter is always a person with a gun. Which answer is best? | Hunters only search for food in a supermarket | * A hunter can be a person, an animal, or someone searching hard for something | Only animals can be hunters | A hunter is always a person with a gun
exam: Jayden asks, «What does hunter mean?» Which answer is best? | Only a shop that sells bargains | A hunter is always an animal | * It depends on the context: a person, an animal that catches other animals, or someone searching hard | Only a person who hunts wild animals
